{"name": "n1102r-04", "sha256": "c54a0f0d145184be95663a8a5bd4e330278a1b73e23a34df9b8ef306acf44a81", "words": 472, "headline": "AI Detected", "prediction_short": "AI", "fraction_ai": 0.905624508857727, "fraction_ai_assisted": 8.795137361461425e-12, "fraction_human": 0.09437547624111176, "version": "4.1", "source": "new", "dashboard_link": "https://www.pangram.com/history/8a5c6453-c6f1-4ab3-b713-51e54e3550f2", "utc": "2026-11-02T19:44:40Z", "windows": [["AI-Generated", "Low", 1, 0, 2, "C."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 25, 2, 186, " The “Hardened” Circuit: Dynorphin & DeltaFosB\nTo protect itself from the Glutamate storm, the brain eventually releases Dynorphin, a kind of chemical blanket that suppresses dopamine."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 17, 186, 273, " That’s how you end up in the “Void”, all apathy and grayness, unable to feel pleasure."], ["Human Written", "Low", 14, 273, 352, "\nIf you’ve tried SSRIs (antidepressants) and they failed you, you’re not crazy."], ["Human Written", "Medium", 18, 352, 459, " Ipser & Stein’s 2012 study showed that Prozac had zero effect on male combat veterans with calcified PTSD."], ["Human Written", "Low", 13, 459, 556, " And the side effects are well-known, including anhedonia, zombification, and sexual dysfunction."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 113, 556, 1254, "\nThey don’t work on calcified PTSD because standard serotonin drugs treat the “software” (mood) and can’t get through to the “hardware”, the structural changes in the amygdala caused by severe trauma. This protocol uses Ketones and HDAC Inhibitors to remodel that physical structure, the part of the brain that resists standard medication.\nWith chronic cycles, DeltaFosB builds up. It’s a protein switch that permanently alters gene expression to cement the trauma circuitry in place (Vialou, et al, 2010).\nYou can’t just “wait” for this to pass, though. For the unlock, we use “System Reformats” (shrooms or iboga) to stimulate GDNF, which physically rewires the brain around these hardened loops."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 1, 1254, 1257, "\nD."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 64, 1257, 1643, " The “Lagging” System: Toxicity & Hypometabolism (The Fog)\n“Brain Fog” is often a fuel crisis. Trauma causes cerebral insulin resistance, so your neurons are swimming in glucose (sugar) and can’t burn it, like a flooded engine.\nIf the brain can’t burn sugar, we switch fuels: PQQ to boost ATP, and Ketones, which bypass the broken glucose pathways and go straight into the mitochondria."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 7, 1643, 1686, " This turns the lights back on immediately."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 17, 1686, 1786, " We alternate hot and cold showers to boost p131 and heat shock proteins and reduce inflammation.\nE."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 27, 1786, 1959, " The “Save Button”: Memory Reconsolidation\nEvery time you have a flashback, your brain tries to “save” the memory again, and that often reinforces the emotional trauma loop."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 5, 1959, 1984, "\nThe fix is “The Jammer”."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 35, 1984, 2203, " Restoring a memory takes visual processing power, so if you keep your Visual-Spatial Working Memory busy (playing Tetris, say) during the critical window after a flashback, the brain fails to “save” the visual details."], ["AI-Generated", "Medium", 11, 2203, 2277, " The memory is restored, but the emotional “sting” is permanently reduced."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 7, 2277, 2309, "\nTetris needs an app or a phone."], ["AI-Generated", "High", 111, 2309, 2928, " The “Color-Path Connect” method doesn’t, and it works better than simple counting because it forces your brain to map 3D space, which competes directly with the visual “saving” of a traumatic memory.\nHow to play:Pick a color (e.g., Blue).\nTrace a Path: Find every blue object in the room and mentally draw a line connecting them from left to right.\nAdd Complexity: Now, mentally “rotate” those objects in your mind or imagine them changing into a different shape (e.g., “That blue chair is now a blue cube”).\nThe Goal: You must do this for 10–20 minutes immediately after a trigger to “jam” the memory reconsolidation."], ["AI-Generated", "Low", 1, 2928, 2931, "\n+1"]]}
